{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Infra.DirichletL","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.DirichletCharacter.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Infra.Polylogarithm"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.beta3IsLChi4_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.beta3IsLChi4_3","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L52-L62","doc":"**Placeholder, not the identity.** Intended: the classical\n`β(3) = L(χ_4, 3)`, whose proof from Theorem A (via `Im Li_3(i) = β(3)`)\nis in `prop:cyclotomic-l-value-decomposition`.\n\nActually `True`, so it is inhabited by `trivial` and asserts nothing —\nthe identity is *named* here, not stated. Nothing in the corpus references\nthis declaration, so it is inert rather than harmful, but do not read a use\nof it as a use of the identity. Stating it properly needs `β` and `L(χ, s)`\nas Mathlib objects; neither is in scope in this file, which is why the\nplaceholder exists. Tracked as `qou-35zi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.chi4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.chi4","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L46-L50","doc":"`β(3) = L(χ_4, 3)` instance (the chief Catalan-like example).\nHere `χ_4` is the unique non-trivial character mod 4 satisfying\n`χ_4(-1) = -1`; specialised at depth 3 gives Catalan's β(3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.hurwitz_lerch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.hurwitz_lerch","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The Hurwitz-Lerch decomposition holds at every depth `n ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass","kind":"class","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L31-L44","doc":"**Hurwitz-Lerch decomposition (axiomatic form).**\n\nEncodes the manuscript identity\n\n  `L(χ, n) = N^{-n} Σ_{a=1..N-1} χ(a) · ζ_H(n, a/N)`\n\nvia the relation between `L(χ, n)` and the Hurwitz zeta values\n`ζ_H(n, a/N)`.  The full statement is conditional on\n`Polylogarithm.TheoremA` (which identifies the cyclotomic\npolylog values) plus the Gauss-sum identity on `χ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.lValueAxiomatic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.lValueAxiomatic","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L21-L29","doc":"Axiomatic Dirichlet L-value `L(χ, n)` for a character `χ mod K`\nand integer `n ≥ 2`.  Encoded as an *axiomatic real number*\nparameterised by the character data (here: just `K` and the\nlist of character values, supplied as a function\n`chi : ℕ → ℝ`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}